**EXCERPT FROM THE MANUFACTURING AND QUALITY CONTROL AGREEMENT**

**THIS MANUFACTURING AND QUALITY CONTROL AGREEMENT** (“Agreement”) is made and entered into as of this 1st day of April, 2023, by and between:

**ACME Manufacturing Solutions, Inc.** (hereinafter referred to as “ACME”), a corporation organized under the laws of the State of Delaware, with its principal office located at 123 Industrial Drive, Wilmington, DE 19801, and

**Precision Parts Co.** (hereinafter referred to as “Precision”), a corporation organized under the laws of the State of Michigan, with its principal office located at 456 Production Lane, Detroit, MI 48201.

**RECITALS**

WHEREAS, ACME operates a series of manufacturing facilities located in Wilmington, Delaware; Nashville, Tennessee; and Austin, Texas (collectively referred to as the “Facilities”);

WHEREAS, ACME specializes in the production of high-quality automotive components, including but not limited to engine parts, transmission systems, and electronic control units (“ECUs”);

WHEREAS, Precision is engaged in the supply of precision tooling and industrial equipment, offering services that include design, fabrication, and maintenance of production lines;

WHEREAS, both parties recognize the importance of adhering to stringent quality control measures to ensure the consistent production of high-quality products;

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements set forth herein, the parties agree as follows:

**1. DEFINITIONS**

1.1 “Production Line” shall mean the sequence of processes and machinery utilized in the manufacturing of automotive components at the Facilities.

1.2 “Quality Control” (“QC”) shall refer to the systematic processes employed to ensure that products meet specified requirements and standards.

1.3 “Industrial Equipment” shall encompass all machinery and tools utilized in the production processes, including CNC machines, robotic arms, and assembly fixtures.

1.4 “ISO 9001” shall refer to the international standard for quality management systems (QMS) that both parties agree to adhere to.

**2. SCOPE OF WORK**

2.1 ACME shall utilize Precision’s industrial equipment, specifically the **Model 5000 CNC Machine** and the **Robotic Assembly Arm Series X**, to enhance production efficiencies at its Wilmington Facility.

2.2 Precision shall be responsible for the installation and calibration of the specified industrial equipment, to be completed by June 15, 2023.

2.3 Quality control processes will be established by ACME and reviewed by Precision’s Quality Assurance Manager, **Ms. Rachel Green**, on a quarterly basis.

**3. MANUFACTURING PROCESS**

3.1 The production of engine components shall commence on July 1, 2023, with an initial output target of 5,000 units per month, subject to adjustments based on demand fluctuations.

3.2 The following production lines shall be operational: 
   - **Line A**: Engine Block Manufacturing
   - **Line B**: Transmission Assembly
   - **Line C**: ECU Integration

3.3 Each production line will be assigned a line supervisor; **Mr. John Taylor** for Line A, **Ms. Lisa Nguyen** for Line B, and **Mr. Samir Patel** for Line C.

**4. QUALITY CONTROL MEASURES**

4.1 ACME shall implement a quality control system compliant with ISO 9001 standards, which will include:
   - Incoming material inspections performed by **Quality Inspector** **Mr. David Lee**.
   - In-process inspections conducted by the production line supervisors.
   - Final product testing by the **Quality Assurance Team**, led by **Ms. Rachel Green**.

4.2 Any product failing to meet the established quality standards shall be documented in a Non-Conformance Report (NCR) and reviewed during the monthly Quality Management Review (QMR).

4.3 The NCRs shall be submitted to the ACME Quality Director, **Dr. Emily Carter**, for corrective action and root cause analysis.

**5. RESPONSIBILITIES OF THE PARTIES**

5.1 ACME agrees to:
   - Provide Precision with access to the Facilities for installation and maintenance of the industrial equipment.
   - Ensure that all production staff are trained on the operational use of the new equipment.

5.2 Precision agrees to:
   - Deliver all necessary equipment, including the **Precision Tooling System**, by May 1, 2023.
   - Provide ongoing technical support and maintenance services for a period of two (2) years post-installation.

**6. PAYMENT TERMS**

6.1 ACME shall compensate Precision a total fee of **$500,000**, payable in the following installments:
   - $200,000 upon signing of this Agreement.
   - $150,000 upon successful installation of the industrial equipment.
   - $150,000 following the first successful quality audit conducted by **ISO Certification Agency** on or before August 31, 2023.

**7. CONFIDENTIALITY**

7.1 Both parties acknowledge that the terms of this Agreement and the proprietary information exchanged, including production techniques, quality control processes, and equipment specifications, shall remain confidential.

7.2 Disclosure of confidential information shall only occur with prior written consent from the disclosing party, except as required by law.

**8. TERM AND TERMINATION**

8.1 This Agreement shall commence on the effective date and shall remain in effect for a period of three (3) years, unless terminated earlier in accordance with this clause.

8.2 Either party may terminate this Agreement with thirty (30) days’ written notice if the other party materially breaches any terms herein and fails to cure such breach within said notice period.

**9. INDEMNIFICATION**

9.1 Each party agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other party, its officers, employees, and agents from any claims, damages, losses, or expenses arising out of the performance of this Agreement, except where caused by the gross negligence or willful misconduct of the indemnified party.

**10. GOVERNING LAW**

10.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict of law principles.

**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the parties have executed this Manufacturing and Quality Control Agreement as of the day and year first above written.

